        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mario Lemieux\n- Organizations: Pittsburgh Penguins, Chicago Blackhawks, Comeback Kid\n- Events: 1992 Stanley Cup Finals\n- Topics: NHL comeback reference\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1992 Stanley Cup Finals, the Chicago Blackhawks took an early 4–1 lead in Game 1 before Mario Lemieux and the Pittsburgh Penguins came back to win the game.\n- In the 1992 Stanley Cup Finals, the Pittsburgh Penguins swept the Chicago Blackhawks in four games and won their second consecutive and second overall Stanley Cup.\n- Mario Lemieux was born on October 5, 1965, and he is a Canadian former professional ice hockey player.\n- Mario Lemieux is the current owner of the Pittsburgh Penguins.\n- The band Comeback Kid took its name from a newspaper headline about Mario Lemieux returning to the NHL.",
